  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Fahim Mohd. Ibrahim And ... vs The State Of Maharashtra on 12 August, 2022",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "4. It has been argued by the learned counsel for the applicants that Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code would not attract in the case of Gutka. False allegations have been levelled against the applicants that they are supplier of Gutka. 3. The learned counsel for the applicants has vehemently argued that there is no direct evidence against the applicants that they were involved in the illegal supply of Gutka. Gutka is not harmful to the life except the surmises of the officers from the Food Safety Department. There are no elements to attract Section 328 of the 925-ABA-1028-22 Indian Penal Code in the present case. Therefore, the anticipatory bail may be granted to the applicants. 4. The learned A.P.P. has strongly opposed the application contending that the applicants were the suppliers of Gutka. The offence is serious. 5. The allegations against the applicants have been made that the co-accused told the Investigating Officer that the applicants had supplied Gutka to him.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. It has been argued by the learned counsel for the applicants that Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code would not attract in the case of Gutka. False allegations have been levelled against the applicants that they are supplier of Gutka. 3. The learned counsel for the applicants has vehemently argued that there is no direct evidence against the applicants that they were involved in the illegal supply of Gutka. Gutka is not harmful to the life except the surmises of the officers from the Food Safety Department. There are no elements to attract Section 328 of the 925-ABA-1028-22 Indian Penal Code in the present case. Therefore, the anticipatory bail may be granted to the applicants. 4. The learned A.P.P. has strongly opposed the application contending that the applicants were the suppliers of Gutka. The offence is serious.",
    "respondent_arguments": "5. The allegations against the applicants have been made that the co-accused told the Investigating Officer that the applicants had supplied Gutka to him.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
